It seems that we found a nice bug (feature ?) in NetHack with which one
can get very rich. The thing happens when a monster dies. If it didn't have
any gold nothing happens, but when it did carry gold this gold is left
behind plus a little extra is added. This is probably to prevent that you
could determine the precise amount with a stethoscope.

You can use this knowledge by throwing one gold piece to a 'greedy' monster
(like orcs, dragons and dwarfs), before killing them. If you kill him
afterwards, he'll leave behind a larger amount. If he already had some money
nothing happens. The extra amount is dungeon level times a random number
between 0 and 30, so for example on level 50 that'll be an extra 750 zorkmids!
Another example: suppose 5 orcs on level 10: hand each orc 1 zorkmid
and kill them afterwards. Extra money: 5 (orcs) * 10 (level) * 15 (average)
is 750 zorkmids.

This extra money could be handy when being in the vicinity of a priest, so
you can buy yourself some extra protection, or when  on a level with a nice
shop which you don't want to rob.

Disclaimer: I only heard this, I didn't check it and I am not sure which PL
            is involved. It is on a Unix system and at least PL9 (maybe PL10).
